Backport JDK-8281525: Enable Zc:strictStrings flag in Visual Studio build

Upstream turned on /Zc:strictStrings, which makes cl.exe treat string literals
as const the way the standard says, and fixed everything that broke. clang has
always been strict, so those same places fail here:

  security.cpp:1288: error: assigning to 'PVOID' (aka 'void *') from
  incompatible type 'const wchar_t[9]'

Taking the commit gets all three AcquireCredentialsHandle package names in
sspi.cpp at once, which is where cycle 8 spent a build on one of them, plus
os_windows.cpp's path prefix, security.cpp's dump() and certificate chain, and
the OID cast.

Two parts of the upstream commit are left out. The flags-cflags.m4 hunk adds
/Zc:strictStrings to the microsoft toolchain, which this build never uses, and
test/hotspot/gtest/runtime/test_os_windows.cpp belongs to the gtest tests that
are switched off here. libwixhelper.cpp does not exist in 11.

Upstream: https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8281525

